-- title:
--   Transversality of L₀ (m/ℓ)P against the level structure
-- statement:
--   Let $q,q'$ be primes with $q'\neq q$, let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ be such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'` (that is, $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the completed algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q\in v$ or $q'\in v$), let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order, $\iota$ an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map into $M_2(\mathbb R)$, $N$ a nonzero squarefree integer prime to $qq'$, and $R\subseteq\Lambda$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$ in the first). Let $J'\supseteq\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule with $\Lambda J'\subseteq J'$, $NJ'\subseteq\Lambda$, $[J':\Lambda]=N^2$, and, for $x\in\Lambda$, $x\in R$ iff $J'x\subseteq J'$. Let $\ell$ be a prime distinct from $q,q'$ and $t\in R$ with $\mathrm{nrd}\,t=\ell$ and $\ell J'+\Lambda t=J't$ elementwise. Assume given, for each fake elliptic curve $E$ over $\mathbb C$ of level $N$, a lattice $\mathrm{latt}\,E\subseteq\mathbb C^2$ and a bijection $e_E$ from the complex points of $E$ (sections of `E.f` over the identity of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb C$) to $\mathbb C^2/\mathrm{latt}\,E$, such that $\mathrm{latt}\,E$ is spanned over $\mathbb Z$ by an $\mathbb R$-basis of $\mathbb C^2$ and is stable under $v\mapsto\iota(x)v$ for $x\in\Lambda$, $e_E$ is additive for the group law, and $e_E$ carries the action of $x\in\Lambda$ to multiplication by $\iota(x)$; and a second family $\mathrm{lattLev}\,E$ whose elements are exactly the classes $e_E(P)$ of points $P$ factoring through `E.lev`, containing $\mathrm{latt}\,E$, stable under $\iota(\Lambda)$, with $N\,\mathrm{lattLev}\,E\subseteq\mathrm{latt}\,E$ and relative index $N^2$. Let $m\neq0$ with $\ell\mid m$, let $E$ be such a curve with a full level-$m$ structure $P$, let $\tau$ lie in the upper half-plane and $c\neq0$ satisfy $c\cdot\mathrm{latt}\,E=\iota(\Lambda)\binom{\tau}{1}$ and $c\cdot\mathrm{lattLev}\,E=\iota(J')\binom{\tau}{1}$, let $v_P$ represent $e_E(P.P)$ with $c\,v_P=m^{-1}\iota(w)\binom{\tau}{1}$ for some $w$, and let $L_0$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule with $\Lambda t=\ell\Lambda+(L_0\cap\Lambda)w$ elementwise. Then for every algebraically closed field $k$, every ring homomorphism $\mathbb C\to k$ and every $x\in\Lambda\cap L_0$: if the point obtained by applying the action of $x$ to $(m/\ell)$ times the base change of $P.P$ to the geometric point factors through `E.lev`, then that point is the identity section at the geometric point.
--
--   This is the transversality statement at the auxiliary prime $\ell$ in the complex-analytic description of fake elliptic curves with level structure: the $\ell$-isogeny line cut out by $L_0$ inside the $(m/\ell)$-torsion generated by a full level-$m$ structure meets the chosen level subscheme only in the origin. It is used in the construction of algebraic families with extra level over the fine moduli problem for Shimura curves attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra.
